### Requires: docker compose up -d  (Keycloak on :8180) and the app running on :8080 with the demo profile
###   mvn spring-boot:run -Dspring-boot.run.profiles=demo  (seeds the customers used below)
@keycloak = http://localhost:8180/realms/customer-realm/protocol/openid-connect/token
@api = http://localhost:8080/api/customers

### ---------- Authentication ----------

### Obtain token: ada.admin (customer-admin)
# @name admin
POST {{keycloak}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=customer-api-client&username=ada.admin&password=password

### Obtain token: sally.sales (customer-reader, department=sales)
# @name salesReader
POST {{keycloak}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=customer-api-client&username=sally.sales&password=password

### Obtain token: nora.norole (valid token, no role)
# @name noRole
POST {{keycloak}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=customer-api-client&username=nora.norole&password=password

### Access without token -> 401
GET {{api}}

### Valid token but no role -> 403
GET {{api}}
Authorization: Bearer {{noRole.response.body.access_token}}

### ---------- customer-reader ----------

### List customers -> 200, only department "sales"
GET {{api}}
Authorization: Bearer {{salesReader.response.body.access_token}}

### Read customer of own department (id 1 = sales) -> 200
GET {{api}}/1
Authorization: Bearer {{salesReader.response.body.access_token}}

### Read customer of other department (id 4 = marketing) -> 403
GET {{api}}/4
Authorization: Bearer {{salesReader.response.body.access_token}}

### Try to create a customer -> 403
POST {{api}}
Authorization: Bearer {{salesReader.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"firstName":"Not","lastName":"Allowed","email":"not.allowed@example.com","status":"ACTIVE","department":"sales"}

### Try to delete a customer -> 403
DELETE {{api}}/1
Authorization: Bearer {{salesReader.response.body.access_token}}

### ---------- customer-admin (CRUD) ----------

### List all customers (all departments) -> 200
GET {{api}}
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.access_token}}

### Create -> 201
# @name created
POST {{api}}
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"firstName":"Max","lastName":"Mustermann","email":"max.mustermann@example.com","status":"ACTIVE","department":"sales"}

### Read -> 200
GET {{api}}/{{created.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.access_token}}

### Update -> 200
PUT {{api}}/{{created.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"firstName":"Max","lastName":"Mustermann","email":"max.mustermann@example.com","status":"INACTIVE","department":"marketing"}

### Delete -> 204
DELETE {{api}}/{{created.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.access_token}}

### Read deleted -> 404
GET {{api}}/{{created.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.access_token}}
